+# Course catalog
+
+`GET /api/courses` returns a local training catalog without external services. The twelve fixed fixtures include all modalities and statuses. The endpoint follows the existing anonymous, read-only health route pattern.
+
+## Query parameters
+
+| Parameter | Meaning | Default |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `q` | Case-insensitive substring search across title, summary and tags | No keyword filter |
+| `modality` | Exact enum: `online`, `in-person`, `hybrid` | All modalities |
+| `status` | Exact enum: `draft`, `active`, `retired` | All statuses |
+| `tag` | Case-insensitive exact match against any tag | All tags |
+| `page` | Positive safe integer, up to 9007199254740991 | `1` |
+| `pageSize` | Integer from 1 through 50 | `10` |
+| `sort` | `title`, `createdAt`, or `updatedAt`, ascending | `title` |
+
+Filters combine with AND. Keyword and tag values are trimmed; an empty keyword adds no filter. An empty tag matches no fixtures. Titles sort case-insensitively; equal values use ID as a stable tie-breaker. Dates are ISO strings and sort chronologically. Pagination follows filtering and sorting. A page beyond the last page returns an empty list. Repeated or unknown parameters, empty enum/numeric values, unsafe integers and unsupported enum values return HTTP 400.
+
+## Request
+
+```http
+GET /api/courses?q=security&modality=online&status=active&tag=ai&page=1&pageSize=5&sort=title
+```
+
+## Success response
+
+HTTP 200, `application/json`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "items": [{
+    "id": "course-001",
+    "title": "AI Security Foundations",
+    "summary": "Introductory course on secure AI-assisted development.",
+    "modality": "online",
+    "status": "active",
+    "tags": ["ai", "security"],
+    "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
+    "updatedAt": "2026-06-12T00:00:00.000Z"
+  }],
+  "page": 1,
+  "pageSize": 5,
+  "totalItems": 1,
+  "totalPages": 1
+}
+```
+
+Every course includes the fields above. `totalItems` and `totalPages` describe all filtered results. No matches return HTTP 200 with `items: []`, `totalItems: 0`, and `totalPages: 0`, retaining the requested pagination values.
+
+## Error response
+
+`GET /api/courses?pageSize=51` returns HTTP 400, `application/json`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "error": {
+    "code": "INVALID_QUERY_PARAMETER",
+    "message": "One or more query parameters are invalid.",
+    "details": [{ "field": "pageSize", "message": "pageSize must be between 1 and 50." }]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Validation collects all invalid fields before resolving application services. Numeric query values use decimal digits only; fractions, signs, whitespace and exponent syntax are rejected.
+
+## Validation
+
+After installing the existing locked dependencies, run `pnpm run build --env-mode=loose`, `pnpm --filter @apps/api test`, `pnpm test --env-mode=loose`, `pnpm run lint`, `pnpm run typecheck --env-mode=loose`, and `pnpm run test:arch --env-mode=loose` from the repository root. The API tests use the actual composed Hono application and public application-service exports. The existing acceptance runner additionally starts the Azure Functions host.
+
+The fixture catalog is intentional for this sample. Persistence, catalog writes, authentication changes and new dependencies are outside this task.
